<field name="NAME">arcadeDrive</field>
<comment pinned="false" h="121" w="612">This takes input from the joysticks, and applies power to the left and right drive motor to move the robot as requested by the driver. "arcade" refers to the control style we're using here. Much like a classic arcade game, when you move the left joystick forward both motors work to drive the robot forward, and when you move the right joystick left and right both motors work to rotate the robot. Combinations of these inputs can be used to create more complex maneuvers.</comment>
<data>{"commentPositionLeft":-312,"commentPositionTop":-307}</data>
